# SQWease — rules for AI assistants

## Project info
- Name: SQWease (Speak Quite Well with Ease)
- Status: early development; Japanese app on `main`, multi-language UI + starter
  decks on branches (see `README.md` "Status")
- Stack: HTML5, CSS3, vanilla JavaScript; Node build scripts; no runtime deps
- Last updated: 2026-10-09

## Read first
- `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `ROADMAP.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `AGENTS.md`
- Live backlog: `tickets/INDEX.md`. Specs: `docs/specs/`.
- Durable context: `memory-bank/` (activeContext, progress, color-alignment-theory,
  srs-status).

## Hard rules
- **Gate:** `node scripts/check.js` must pass before committing.
- **Never hand-edit generated files** (`flashcards-vocab.js`, `boxes-data.js`,
  `content/common-kanji.js`, `data/<lang>/vocab.js`). Edit `content/` and rebuild.
- **No runtime dependency** without an ADR in `DECISIONS.md`.
- **No new UI control as a clickable `<div>`** — use a real button/link with a
  name and visible focus.
- **Guard `localStorage` reads** through the safe store helper (UI branch).
- **Keep `file://` working:** core data is script-loaded, never `fetch()`ed.

## Coloring rules
- Color comes only from the first syllable of romaji; JA/romaji/EN inherit it.
- Generic behavior → `syllable-color.js`; Boxes-only rules → `boxes-coloring.js`;
  particle detection → `romaji.js`. Do not add Boxes data to the shared lists.
- Verify on all 5 Boxes tabs and both list/practice after any coloring change.

## Documentation standard
- Markdown; explain the "why"; link between docs.
- Update the affected doc (and the ticket) in the same commit as the work.
- Mark AI-assisted sections (e.g. "AI-scaffolded"), keep claims backed by a run.

## Validation checklist
- [ ] `node scripts/check.js` passes
- [ ] No generated file hand-edited
- [ ] Ticket status/evidence updated
- [ ] `ROADMAP.md`/`ARCHITECTURE.md` updated if the shipped surface or a boundary changed
